    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d403">

                <pb facs="0470" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg452"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/7–1846</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Pawley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/> No. 78</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-18">July 18, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Acting Secretary of State transmits for the confidential information and
                    files of the Embassy copies of a note of even date to the Brazilian Embassy in
                    Washington and of Statement LL–8<anchor n="51" xml:id="d403-f1"/> showing
                    charges made against the Government of Brazil during the period from December 1,
                    1945 through February 28, 1945 [<hi rendition="#italic">1946</hi>], for defense
                    material transferred to Brazil under the Lend-Lease Agreement signed March 3,
                    1942.</p>
                <p>It will be noted that the amount of charges during the period under reference is
                    $796,037.79 and that charges through February 28, 1946 aggregate the grand total
                    of $183,959,349.81. Under the terms of the Agreement a payment of $11,666,666.66
                    is now due.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
